{"author":{"id":"89da5fec8eff6d69dbcdd68f81be7e9163b16f34b17e978ecf3554487379f453"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1773943283,"nonce":"Vb2nB2rf+HN6iik0O2QYGKwlVAM=","title":"P2: API — path resolution, forks endpoint, fork/resume actions","message":"Add server-side path resolution and fork/resume API endpoints.\n\nParent: 86b63bc\nDepends on: 72751b7 (P1 — dag_uuid/dag_parent_uuid must exist)\n\n## Endpoints\n1. GET /api/conversations/:id?leaf=\u003cdag_uuid\u003e — walk dag_parent_uuid backward from leaf to root, return ordered blocks for that path. When leaf is omitted, return current behavior (all blocks by position order, or follow the latest leaf heuristic).\n\n2. GET /api/conversations/:id/forks — return fork points: blocks where multiple children share the same dag_parent_uuid. For each fork point, return { dag_uuid, children: [{ dag_uuid, first_text (first ~60 chars of assistant response), turn_count, branch_index }] }.\n\n3. POST /api/conversations/:id/fork — body: { message_dag_uuid: string }. Import and call sdk.forkSession(sessionId, { upToMessageId: message_dag_uuid }). Wait for ingestion of the new JSONL file (or trigger it). Return { conversation_id, session_id }.\n\n4. POST /api/conversations/:id/resume — body: { message_dag_uuid: string, label?: string }. Create a Console session with: provider_session_id = conversation.session_id, resume_at_message = message_dag_uuid, backend_type = \"sdk\", label = provided or conversation title. Return { console_session_id }.\n\n## Data model\n- ConsoleSession needs new field: resume_at_message?: string (the dag_uuid to resume from)\n- Add to console_sessions table via migration\n- SessionManager.create() accepts resume_at_message in input","files":null}]}